WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们制作《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.960
Hi there.
大家好。

9
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.160
Today, we're going to talk about manager and salesman.
今天，我们要聊聊《经理与销售员》这一集。

10
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.820
We have a huge episode.
这一集内容非常丰富。

11
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.460
It really is.
确实如此。

12
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:39.180
It is Season 6, Episode 16, written by Mindy Kaling and directed by Mark Webb.
这是第六季第十六集，由敏迪·卡灵编剧，马克·韦布执导。

13
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.080
Hit us with a summary, lady.
给我们来个剧情梗概吧，女士。

14
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.000
Here it is.
好的。

15
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.600
Sabre CEO Joe Bennett visits Dunder Mifflin Scranton.
赛博公司的首席执行官乔·贝内特造访了邓德·米夫林斯克兰顿分公司。

16
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:53.020
She brings her two Great Danes, her autobiography, and a lot of new policies.
她带来了两只大丹犬、她的自传以及许多新政策。

17
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:59.100
When she discovers that Michael and Jim are co-managers, she tells them there can only be one manager.
当她发现迈克尔和吉姆是共同经理时，她告诉他们只能留下一位经理。

18
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:05.780
And they have until the end of the day to decide who will be a salesperson and who will stay on as manager.
他们必须在下班前决定谁去做销售员，谁留任经理。

19
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:16.660
Meanwhile, Andy is handing out Valentine's cards to everyone in The Office, which sparks confusion as to where his affections truly lie.
与此同时，安迪给办公室里的每个人都发了情人节贺卡，这让大家对他到底心仪谁感到困惑。

20
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.900
I am telling you, watching Andy and Aaron is making me crazy.
我跟你说，看安迪和艾琳的互动简直让我抓狂。

21
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.500
I just want one of them to just say, I like you.
我真希望他们中有一个人能直接说出“我喜欢你”。

22
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.640
I know, but they have the thing where neither one of them will ask the other one out.
我知道，但他们就是那种谁也不肯先开口约对方的情况。

23
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:28.540
It's making me crazy.
这真的让我抓狂。

24
00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:29.600
It's very sweet.
这很甜蜜。

25
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.360
It is sweet, but it's making me crazy.
确实甜蜜，但真的让我抓狂。

26
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:36.940
Fast fact number one, Kathy Bates is Joe Bennett.
第一个速览事实，凯西·贝茨饰演乔·贝内特。

27
00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.680
Kathy Flippin' Bates.
竟然是凯西·贝茨。

28
00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:45.300
Now, I know she was on last week's episode, but it was via a computer screen.
我知道她上周那一集也出现了，但那是通过电脑屏幕。

29
00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.900
Here she is, live, in person.
而这一次，她是真人亲临现场。

30
00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.840
Walking right next to us, talking to us.
就在我们身边走动，和我们交谈。

31
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:59.220
You know, Kathy Bates is one of just a few actors who have been nominated for the triple crown of acting.
你们知道吗，凯西·贝茨是少数几位获得过表演“大满贯”提名的演员之一。

32
00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:07.080
That means that she has been nominated for a Tony for her work on the stage, an Academy Award for film, an Emmy for television.
这意味着她曾因舞台表演获得托尼奖提名，因电影获得奥斯卡奖提名，因电视作品获得艾美奖提名。

33
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:14.260
By the way, she has won an Academy Award, two Golden Globes, two SAG Awards, and two Emmy Awards.
顺便提一下，她还获得过一座奥斯卡奖、两座金球奖、两座演员工会奖和两座艾美奖。

34
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:19.860
Her nominations for awards were so many that I actually got confused.
她的获奖提名多到让我都搞糊涂了。

35
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.040
I couldn't even track them all.
我根本数不过来。

36
00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.200
It's so many.
实在太多了。

37
00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.660
Yeah, so you guys, we were a little nervous.
是啊，所以大家，我们当时有点紧张。

38
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:33.400
I mean, this acting legend came in to our job.
我是说，这位表演界的传奇人物来到了我们的工作场所。

39
00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.000
We got a lot of mail, Angela, asking what was our reaction to having Kathy Bates.
安吉拉，我们收到了很多邮件，问我们见到凯西·贝茨时是什么反应。

40
00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.460
I mean, I think you just heard it.
我想你们刚才已经听到了。

41
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.540
We were so excited, but I was really nervous.
我们非常兴奋，但我真的很紧张。

42
00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:43.680
I was intimidated.
我感到很有压力。

43
00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.540
Yeah, but not by anything other than just her presence, because she's very lovely, you know.
是啊，但并不是因为别的，仅仅是因为她的气场，因为她本人非常可爱，你们懂的。

44
00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:50.060
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

45
00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:50.580
She was so nice to everyone.
她对每个人都非常好。

46
00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.400
Oh, my gosh, yes.
天哪，确实。

47
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.120
She's super down to earth and kind.
她超级平易近人，而且很友善。

48
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:53.620
Yeah.
没错。

49
00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:57.780
But her legacy that followed her into the room was massive.
但她带进房间的那种传奇光环依然非常强大。

50
00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.940
Yes, she had this quiet power as she walked in the room.
是的，她走进房间时自带一种沉静的力量。

51
00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:04.420
I was so, like, nervous to say anything to her.
我当时特别紧张，不知道该怎么跟她开口。

52
00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:09.900
You know, my hair colorist of over 20 years, Robert Hickland, I love this man,
你知道，我那合作了二十多年的染发师罗伯特·希克兰，我超爱他，

53
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:15.260
he told me once that he also colored Kathy Bates' hair once.
他有次跟我说，他也给凯西·贝茨染过头发。

54
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:15.780
What?
什么？

55
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.480
This was before Kathy was on our show.
那是在凯西上我们节目之前的事了。

56
00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.900
He said, oh, I don't know how she came up.
他说，噢，我不记得是怎么聊到她的了。

57
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.980
But he was like, I colored her hair once.
但他就是说，我给她的头发染过色。

58
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.640
And when he told me that, I was floored.
当他告诉我这件事时，我简直惊呆了。

59
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.480
And now here she was.
而现在，她就在这儿。

60
00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.240
She had come in.
她进来了。

61
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.700
And I remember that I was sitting at the reception desk.
我记得当时我正坐在接待台那儿。

62
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:37.060
And it was like, I wanted to be like, my hairdresser did your hair once.
我当时就想说，我的发型师给你染过头发。

63
00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:37.440
No.
不行。

64
00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:37.940
Like, I.
就像，我。

65
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.640
Suppress, suppress.
忍住，忍住。

66
00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:40.500
Don't say it.
别说出来。

67
00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:40.820
Yes, yes.
对，对。

68
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.620
But I was like, moment of connection.
但我当时就觉得，这是一个建立联系的时刻。

69
00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.360
I have something in common with you.
我和你有共同点。

70
00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.880
The same man has colored her hair.
同一个人给我们的头发染过色。

71
00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.580
That is what I was so nervous.
这就是我当时那么紧张的原因。

72
00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.480
And I had to, like, make sure I didn't do that.
我得确保自己没把这话说出口。

73
00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:55.300
I do think that, like, eventually by day three, I did tell her that tidbit.
我觉得，大概到了第三天，我还是把这个小八卦告诉她了。

74
00:03:55.780 --> 00:04:00.100
And it was, you know, the response you would expect, which was, oh.
然后，你知道，反应正如你所料，就是，噢。

75
00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:03.660
Anyway.
总之。

76
00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:09.160
Kathy Bates was on Anderson when Anderson Cooper had his own talk show.
凯西·贝茨曾上过安德森·库珀主持的脱口秀节目。

77
00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.620
And she talked about being on The Office.
她谈到了出演《办公室》的经历。

78
00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.920
And I thought we could give it a listen.
我想我们可以听听看。

79
00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:17.820
How was it like working with the comedy ensemble versus the cast on Harry's Law?
和《办公室》的喜剧团队合作，与《律政俏师太》的剧组相比，感觉如何？

80
00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.860
Well, I was so in awe of Steve Carell, you know.
嗯，我对史蒂夫·卡瑞尔非常敬佩，你知道的。

81
00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.760
And actually, I had worked with Rainn Wilson.
而且实际上，我和雷恩·威尔森合作过。

82
00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.340
I actually cast him when I was directing an episode of Six Feet Under.
我在执导《六尺之下》的一集时，其实是我选的他。

83
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:27.900
Oh, really?
噢，真的吗？

84
00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.120
Way, way back.
很久很久以前了。

85
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:29.420
Of course.
当然。

86
00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.720
He was great on Six Feet Under.
他在《六尺之下》里表现得很棒。

87
00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:31.020
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

88
00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:31.780
He was terrific.
他非常出色。

89
00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:39.700
And so it's been wonderful to watch him on The Office just knock it out of the ballpark all the time.
所以看到他在《办公室》里一直表现得那么精彩，真是太棒了。

90
00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.940
But it was great to work with Steve Carell.
能和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔合作真的很棒。

91
00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.020
And I loved working with the two great Danes.
而且我很喜欢和那两位伟大的丹麦人合作。

92
00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.060
That was a lot of fun.
那真的很有趣。

93
00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.020
So I didn't know this until I saw this clip.
所以直到看到这段视频，我才知道这件事。

94
00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:54.900
She has actually directed a ton of television, including five episodes of Six Feet Under.
她其实执导过大量的电视作品，包括五集《六尺之下》。

95
00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:58.520
And like she said, she directed Rainn Wilson.
就像她说的，她执导过雷恩·威尔森。

96
00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.840
So I reached out to Rainn.
所以我联系了雷恩。

97
00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:01.880
Oh, you did?
噢，你联系了？

98
00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:02.300
Yeah.
是啊。

99
00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.860
And he described the experience as a, quote, double whammy.
他把那次经历形容为，引用他的话，双重打击。

100
00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:11.940
He said, I got a major role on one of the deepest, most respected TV shows going on.
他说，我当时在一部最深刻、最受推崇的电视节目中获得了一个重要角色。

101
00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.960
It was on HBO, no less.
那可是HBO出品的剧。

102
00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:18.200
And at the same time, I was being directed by an Oscar winner.
与此同时，我还在一位奥斯卡得主的执导下演戏。

103
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.440
He said it was a dream come true that she was an excellent director.
他说能由她执导简直是梦想成真，她是一位出色的导演。

104
00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:26.720
He said they rehearsed a lot and she gave great notes, which, of course, wasn't surprising.
他说他们排练了很多次，她给出的建议也非常棒，当然，这并不令人意外。

105
00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:34.600
But he said he was definitely quite intimidated, which made him act very formal and somewhat awkward around her.
但他表示自己确实感到相当紧张，这让他跟她相处时表现得非常拘谨，甚至有些笨拙。

106
00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.440
Wait, more awkward than usual for Rainn?
等等，比平时的雷恩还要笨拙？

107
00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.120
Exactly.
没错。

108
00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:42.840
But he said this was actually perfect for the character he was playing.
但他表示这对于他当时饰演的角色来说其实非常完美。

109
00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:43.860
Oh, right.
哦，也是。

110
00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:49.160
But the very first episode that he did of Six Feet Under was directed by Kathy Bates.
但他参演的第一集《六尺之下》就是由凯西·贝茨执导的。

111
00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:54.740
So she was a big part of picking him for that role that became a major recurring role for him.
所以她在挑选他出演那个后来成为他重要常驻角色的过程中起到了很大作用。

112
00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:55.320
Wow.
哇。

113
00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.680
So she was a pivotal person in his life.
所以她是他人生的关键人物。

114
00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:58.120
Yeah.
没错。

115
00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:58.960
In his career.
在他职业生涯中的关键人物。

116
00:05:59.200 --> 00:05:59.540
Yes.
是的。

117
00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:00.540
That is so cool.
那太酷了。

118
00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:06.760
Well, fast fact number two, Kathy mentioned, on Anderson, the Great Danes.
好了，第二个小知识，凯西在安德森的节目里提到了大丹犬。

119
00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.680
I remember the Great Danes.
我记得那些大丹犬。

120
00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.540
How could we forget the Great Danes?
我们怎么可能忘记那些大丹犬呢？

121
00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.680
Two small, like ponies were on set with us.
有两只像小马一样大的狗和我们一起在片场。

122
00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.760
Yes, and on set with us a lot.
是的，而且经常和我们一起在片场。

123
00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:25.120
Randy Cordray said that we once again went to Bob Dunn's Animal Services and their head trainer, Denise Sanders, came through for us.
兰迪·科德雷说我们再次找到了鲍勃·邓恩动物服务公司，他们的首席训练师丹妮丝·桑德斯帮了我们大忙。

124
00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.520
The dogs' names were Gabby and Guinness.
那两只狗的名字叫加比和吉尼斯。

125
00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:33.460
He said they were truly majestic, gorgeous, and very well-disciplined.
他说它们真的非常威严、漂亮，而且训练有素。

126
00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.640
I remember that.
我记得那件事。

127
00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:35.740
They were really amazing.
它们真的很棒。

128
00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:43.440
Incidentally, David Denman had a Great Dane who I spent quite a bit of time with.
顺便提一下，大卫·丹曼有一只大丹犬，我花了不少时间跟它相处。

129
00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:50.600
And I remember this thing where David Denman told me that Great Danes are great apartment dogs.
我记得大卫·丹曼当时跟我说，大丹犬是非常适合在公寓养的狗。

130
00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:51.760
How so?
怎么说？

131
00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:57.020
He said they're just really, really chill and they actually don't need a lot of exercise.
他说它们真的非常冷静，其实不需要太多的运动。

132
00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:00.000
That a lot of smaller dogs are far more active.
很多小型犬反而要活跃得多。

133
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.960
They need to go out.
它们需要出门。

134
00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.140
They need walking.
它们需要遛弯。

135
00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.400
But Great Danes are kind of like just big loungers.
但大丹犬就像是那种大型的“躺平族”。

136
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:06.880
That makes sense.
这倒说得通。

137
00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.500
You know, my little chihuahua mixes, they get what we call the zoomies.
你知道，我的吉娃娃混种犬，它们会有我们所谓的“疯狂冲刺”。

138
00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:11.260
Yes.
是的。

139
00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.680
Where they zoom around and run and run and run in a circle.
就是它们会绕着圈不停地跑啊跑啊跑。

140
00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:16.900
Maggie is a large dog.
玛吉是一只大狗。

141
00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.800
She's a shepherd mix.
它是牧羊犬混种。

142
00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:19.760
That's Jenna's dog.
那是珍娜的狗。

143
00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.320
It's like eight times the size of my dog.
它体型大概是我家狗的八倍大。

144
00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.980
And Maggie also gets the zoomies.
