大西洋拥有所有的历史。

935
00:41:40.440 --> 00:41:48.060
That is where the amoebas crawled from the murky depths and became man.
那是变形虫从浑浊的深渊中爬出来并进化成人类的地方。

936
00:41:49.140 --> 00:41:50.820
So it's pretty cool.
所以它很酷。

937
00:41:52.020 --> 00:41:52.620
Wow.
哇。

938
00:41:52.860 --> 00:41:54.240
That's what he thinks.
他是这么想的。

939
00:41:55.380 --> 00:41:57.580
Makes me laugh so hard about the Atlantic Ocean.
关于大西洋的这段话让我笑得不行。

940
00:41:57.840 --> 00:42:02.660
He also does this thing in this talking head that, I mean, we all know people.
他在那段采访里还做了件事，我是说，我们都认识这样的人。

941
00:42:02.760 --> 00:42:03.240
That do this.
会这么做的人。

942
00:42:03.380 --> 00:42:04.860
But it never quite makes sense.
但这从来都说不通。

943
00:42:05.860 --> 00:42:08.620
He's like, the Arctic Ocean's too cold.
他说，北冰洋太冷了。

944
00:42:08.800 --> 00:42:09.560
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

945
00:42:09.860 --> 00:42:10.060
Yeah.
是啊。

946
00:42:10.880 --> 00:42:11.940
Well, thank you very much.
嗯，非常感谢。

947
00:42:12.100 --> 00:42:13.080
Like, what?
就像是，什么鬼？

948
00:42:13.720 --> 00:42:15.600
Anyway, that's in the DVDs.
总之，那段在DVD里。

949
00:42:15.680 --> 00:42:16.900
I just thought it was hilarious.
我只是觉得太搞笑了。

950
00:42:17.360 --> 00:42:23.240
I love it that this scene cut away to a talking head of Michael explaining this.
我喜欢这个场景切换到迈克尔解释这一切的采访片段。

951
00:42:23.580 --> 00:42:23.630
Right.
对。

952
00:42:23.740 --> 00:42:25.160
And then cuts back.
然后切回。

953
00:42:25.380 --> 00:42:26.120
To this scene.
这个场景。

954
00:42:26.540 --> 00:42:29.700
Where Oscar finds out why Michael is so happy.
奥斯卡发现了迈克尔为什么这么开心。

955
00:42:30.060 --> 00:42:32.260
He's like, well, maybe I should be a salesperson too.
他说，嗯，也许我也该当个销售。

956
00:42:32.760 --> 00:42:33.080
Yeah.
是啊。

957
00:42:33.180 --> 00:42:34.360
And Michael's like, what are you talking about?
迈克尔就说，你在说什么呢？

958
00:42:34.560 --> 00:42:34.740
Yeah.
是啊。

959
00:42:35.040 --> 00:42:36.760
And he's like, they make way more money.
他说，销售赚的钱多多了。

960
00:42:36.800 --> 00:42:37.780
It's in the manual.
手册里写着呢。

961
00:42:38.300 --> 00:42:39.720
Saber has no cap on commissions.
赛博公司的佣金没有上限。

962
00:42:40.040 --> 00:42:41.420
He read it all in the manual.
他全在手册里读到了。

963
00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:42.960
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

964
00:42:43.160 --> 00:42:43.920
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

965
00:42:44.060 --> 00:42:45.480
Michael has his talking head.
迈克尔开始了他的访谈。

966
00:42:45.620 --> 00:42:49.520
He's like, well, according to the manual, there is no cap on commissions.
他说，嗯，根据手册，佣金确实没有上限。

967
00:42:49.820 --> 00:42:51.000
I have been hustled.
我被坑了。

968
00:42:51.740 --> 00:42:51.920
Yeah.
是啊。

969
00:42:51.920 --> 00:43:01.200
So, Michael is going to walk in on Joe in the conference room, having a meeting with Jim, where Jim is saying he'll be a salesperson.
所以，迈克尔会闯进会议室，当时乔正在和吉姆开会，吉姆正说他要去做销售。

970
00:43:01.320 --> 00:43:02.780
He does my favorite thing too.
他还做了我最喜欢的一个动作。

971
00:43:02.920 --> 00:43:04.420
He whispers, son of a bitch.
他低声骂了一句，该死的。

972
00:43:06.500 --> 00:43:16.580
I want to point out that this conference room went from being a place where we were having a presentation with rows of chairs to now having a table in the middle of it.
我想指出的是，这个会议室从原本摆满椅子进行演示的地方，变成了中间放着一张桌子。

973
00:43:16.580 --> 00:43:27.260
It's gone back and forth between, like, sort of office style for Joe with the conference table to presentation style, and we never see this transformation happen on the show.
它在乔那种带有会议桌的办公室风格和演示风格之间来回切换，我们在剧中从没见过这种转换过程。

974
00:43:27.380 --> 00:43:27.700
Never.
从来没见过。

975
00:43:27.940 --> 00:43:30.320
No one's ever moving a table in and out.
从来没人搬进搬出桌子。

976
00:43:30.460 --> 00:43:32.880
Where does the table go when we're not using it?
不用的时候桌子去哪了？

977
00:43:32.880 --> 00:43:33.740
Who's moving it all?
到底是谁在搬？

978
00:43:33.880 --> 00:43:34.620
Who is it?
是谁呢？

979
00:43:34.620 --> 00:43:40.760
All I want is B-roll of, like, Kevin and whoever, just moving chairs and tables all day.
我只想看一些空镜，比如凯文或者谁，整天就在那搬椅子搬桌子。

980
00:43:40.940 --> 00:43:43.200
I feel like there's a missed opportunity here.
我觉得这错失了一个好机会。

981
00:43:43.560 --> 00:43:50.000
I would love it if, like, Michael designated this to the warehouse guys.
如果迈克尔把这活儿指派给仓库的人，我会很乐意看到的。

982
00:43:50.540 --> 00:43:53.580
And can you imagine just, like, how annoyed every time?
你能想象他们每次有多烦吗？

983
00:43:53.580 --> 00:43:55.560
They have to come up and move everything?
他们得上来把所有东西都搬走？

984
00:43:55.660 --> 00:43:56.000
Yes.
没错。

985
00:43:56.140 --> 00:43:59.640
What if there's just an episode where they're moving it back and forth all day?
如果有一集专门讲他们整天搬来搬去会怎样？

986
00:44:00.020 --> 00:44:00.460
Right.
对。

987
00:44:00.660 --> 00:44:03.860
And Daryl is like, Michael, we have deliveries to make.
然后达里尔说，迈克尔，我们还有货要送呢。

988
00:44:03.860 --> 00:44:08.020
Or Michael pays, like, petty cash to Leo and Gino.
或者迈克尔用零用钱雇了里奥和吉诺。

989
00:44:08.380 --> 00:44:08.940
Yes.
没错。

990
00:44:09.060 --> 00:44:11.680
And they come and move everything from Vance Refrigeration.
他们从万斯制冷公司过来把所有东西都搬走。

991
00:44:12.200 --> 00:44:12.960
Oh, my God.
天哪。

992
00:44:13.120 --> 00:44:13.440
Ugh.
呃。

993
00:44:13.720 --> 00:44:14.300
I know.
我知道。

994
00:44:14.460 --> 00:44:15.900
This is, how does it happen?
这到底是怎么做到的？

995
00:44:16.080 --> 00:44:17.300
Who's the muscle here?
谁是这里的苦力？

996
00:44:17.500 --> 00:44:17.550
How does it happen?
这到底是怎么做到的？

997
00:44:17.720 --> 00:44:18.080
Yes.
没错。

998
00:44:18.500 --> 00:44:21.600
We also had a continuity catch in this scene.
我们在这个场景里还发现了一个连贯性错误。

999
00:44:21.600 --> 00:44:22.460
I did, too.
我也发现了。

1000
00:44:22.760 --> 00:44:23.340
The hair?
头发吗？

1001
00:44:23.520 --> 00:44:23.940
Yes.
没错。

1002
00:44:24.140 --> 00:44:24.620
Yes.
是的。

1003
00:44:24.920 --> 00:44:27.660
You and Jess B from Batesville, Indiana.
你和来自印第安纳州贝茨维尔的杰西·B。

1004
00:44:28.080 --> 00:44:32.520
When Michael and Jim are talking with Joe, Michael messes up Jim's hair,
当迈克尔和吉姆在和乔谈话时，迈克尔弄乱了吉姆的头发，

1005
00:44:32.520 --> 00:44:36.520
and it stays disheveled until the very end when Michael gets up to leave,
直到最后迈克尔起身离开时，头发一直都是乱的，

1006
00:44:36.560 --> 00:44:38.320
and then it is perfectly combed again.
然后又变得梳理得整整齐齐了。

1007
00:44:38.480 --> 00:44:38.860
Yes.
没错。

1008
00:44:39.040 --> 00:44:42.240
At 9 minutes, 13 seconds, messy hair.
在9分13秒时，头发是乱的。

1009
00:44:42.400 --> 00:44:42.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1010
00:44:42.840 --> 00:44:43.800
That's when it starts.
就是从那时候开始的。

1011
00:44:43.980 --> 00:44:50.000
It stays messy until 9.55, and then at 9.58, it's perfectly back to normal.
它一直乱到9分55秒，然后到了9分58秒，又完美地恢复原样了。

1012
00:44:50.380 --> 00:44:50.760
Right?
对吧？

1013
00:44:51.320 --> 00:44:52.080
Nice catch.
观察得很仔细。

1014
00:44:52.480 --> 00:44:56.600
So, in addition to messing up Jim's hair, Michael also messes up Jim's plans.
所以，除了弄乱吉姆的头发，迈克尔还搅乱了吉姆的计划。

1015
00:44:56.860 --> 00:44:57.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1016
00:44:57.380 --> 00:44:58.160
Did you like that segue?
喜欢这个转折吗？

1017
00:44:58.460 --> 00:44:59.700
I just thought of it in the moment.
我刚才灵机一动想到的。

1018
00:44:59.920 --> 00:45:01.160
I'm really kind of proud of it.
我真的还挺得意的。

1019
00:45:01.320 --> 00:45:02.540
You're like a professional.
你简直像个专业人士。

1020
00:45:02.740 --> 00:45:04.040
I feel like I am.
我觉得我确实是。

1021
00:45:04.040 --> 00:45:04.180
You're like a professional.
你简直像个专业人士。

1022
00:45:04.560 --> 00:45:06.420
I mean, after like 100 and something episodes.
我是说，毕竟都拍了一百多集了。

1023
00:45:06.540 --> 00:45:07.840
You're like a wordsmith.
你简直是个文字大师。

1024
00:45:08.200 --> 00:45:08.640
Thank you.
谢谢。

1025
00:45:08.860 --> 00:45:09.080
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1026
00:45:09.080 --> 00:45:13.740
Basically, Michael says, you know, I think I want to be the salesperson.
基本上，迈克尔说，你知道吗，我想做销售。

1027
00:45:13.940 --> 00:45:15.740
And Joe says, you know what, Michael?
然后乔说，你知道吗，迈克尔？

1028
00:45:15.940 --> 00:45:17.960
You have more experience across the board.
你在各方面都有更丰富的经验。

1029
00:45:18.100 --> 00:45:19.000
You've been in sales.
你做过销售。

1030
00:45:19.140 --> 00:45:19.940
You've been a manager.
你也做过经理。

1031
00:45:20.220 --> 00:45:22.580
I'm going to defer to your judgment on this.
这件事我听你的判断。

1032
00:45:22.880 --> 00:45:30.180
And he takes the sales position, and now he's got to move in all his stuff to Jim's little desk.
于是他接手了销售职位，现在他得把所有东西搬到吉姆的小办公桌那儿。

1033
00:45:30.180 --> 00:45:32.980
And Jim is now moving into Michael's office.
而吉姆现在要搬进迈克尔的办公室。

1034
00:45:33.560 --> 00:45:33.900
Yes.
没错。

1035
00:45:34.140 --> 00:45:35.300
You see Jim and Pam.
你看到了吉姆和帕姆。

1036
00:45:35.660 --> 00:45:37.480
Jim is the manager now.
吉姆现在是经理了。

1037
00:45:37.880 --> 00:45:42.060
At 10 minutes, 6 seconds, you're going to get a real good shot of belly bump E.
在10分06秒时，你会看到一个非常清晰的孕肚特写。

1038
00:45:42.560 --> 00:45:45.760
This was a very large belly bump that I had to wear.
我当时不得不戴上一个非常大的假孕肚。

1039
00:45:46.320 --> 00:45:47.920
Pam has gone up a bump.
帕姆的肚子又大了一圈。

1040
00:45:48.120 --> 00:45:50.400
Well, she's getting into her last trimester.
嗯，她快进入孕晚期了。

1041
00:45:50.660 --> 00:45:50.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1042
00:45:51.060 --> 00:45:53.100
Next week, she's giving birth, everybody.
下周，她就要生了，各位。

1043
00:45:53.380 --> 00:45:53.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1044
00:45:54.180 --> 00:45:55.880
Well, Dwight is not pleased at all.
德怀特对此一点也不高兴。

1045
00:45:56.180 --> 00:45:58.360
He makes a phone call to Bobcat.
他给“山猫”打了个电话。

1046
00:45:58.660 --> 00:45:59.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1047
00:45:59.180 --> 00:46:00.320
Bobcat, this is Dragon.
山猫，我是龙。

1048
00:46:00.900 --> 00:46:03.200
Meet me by the dumpster in 90 seconds.
90秒后在垃圾桶旁见。

1049
00:46:03.460 --> 00:46:05.660
And he hangs up and goes, 89, 88.
然后他挂了电话说，89，88。

1050
00:46:07.980 --> 00:46:12.700
20 minutes later, Ryan meets him outside by the dumpsters.
20分钟后，瑞安在垃圾桶旁见到了他。

1051
00:46:13.020 --> 00:46:14.940
Do you mean scarf-y Ryan?
你是说“围巾瑞安”吗？

1052
00:46:15.400 --> 00:46:17.620
Because I'm calling him scarf-y Ryan.
因为我管他叫“围巾瑞安”。

1053
00:46:17.760 --> 00:46:18.740
Such a scarf.
真是条围巾。

1054
00:46:19.000 --> 00:46:20.280
A turquoise scarf.
一条绿松石色的围巾。

1055
00:46:20.520 --> 00:46:25.760
You know, in the shooting draft, because I reread it, Joe Bennett says, nice scarf.
你知道吗，在拍摄剧本里，因为我重读了一遍，乔·贝内特说，好漂亮的围巾。

1056
00:46:26.040 --> 00:46:26.440
Oh!
噢！

1057
00:46:26.440 --> 00:46:29.380
She comments on a scarf earlier in the episode.
她在剧集早些时候评论过那条围巾。

1058
00:46:29.580 --> 00:46:33.180
But yeah, if you want to see scarf-y, go to 10 minutes, 32 seconds.
不过说真的，如果你想看“围巾瑞安”，请跳转到10分32秒。

1059
00:46:33.660 --> 00:46:36.180
They have this hilarious dialogue, too.
他们还有一段超搞笑的对话。

1060
00:46:36.540 --> 00:46:39.360
When Ryan says, did you see Saw?
当瑞安问，你看过《电锯惊魂》吗？

1061
00:46:39.740 --> 00:46:41.260
And Dwight goes, of course I see Saw.
德怀特回答，我当然看过《电锯惊魂》（Saw）。

1062
00:46:41.520 --> 00:46:43.000
Moe's and I see Saw all the time.
莫和我都经常看《电锯惊魂》。

1063
00:46:43.400 --> 00:46:43.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1064
00:46:43.860 --> 00:46:45.280
He's like, no, the movie Saw.
他说，不，是电影《电锯惊魂》。

1065
00:46:45.840 --> 00:46:49.800
Because they still have their diabolical plan to take down Jim.
因为他们当时还在策划那个搞垮吉姆的邪恶计划。

1066
00:46:49.800 --> 00:46:56.940
And Ryan's idea is that, what, they're going to kidnap Jim and, like, do psychological torture on him?
瑞安的想法是，什么，他们要绑架吉姆，然后对他进行心理折磨？

1067
00:46:57.200 --> 00:46:58.740
Dwight rejects the idea.
德怀特拒绝了这个想法。

1068
00:46:59.140 --> 00:46:59.780
He does.
他确实拒绝了。

1069
00:46:59.880 --> 00:47:01.280
He's like, this is not a good idea.
他说，这主意可不怎么样。

1070
00:47:01.700 --> 00:47:06.480
I do want to say in this scene, a nice touch at 10 minutes, 30 seconds.
我想提一下这个场景，10分30秒处有个很棒的细节。

1071
00:47:06.480 --> 00:47:11.100
That's some nice, fakie snow on the dumpster, kind of around.
垃圾桶周围那些看起来很逼真的假雪。

1072
00:47:11.420 --> 00:47:15.800
It was provided by Ron Neri's team from A&A Special Effects.
那是罗恩·内里团队提供的，来自A&A特效公司。

1073
00:47:16.360 --> 00:47:19.360
Again, they had to bring in a small truckload of ice.
再说一次，他们得运来一小卡车的冰。

1074
00:47:19.360 --> 00:47:23.520
It was delivered from Union Ice of North Hollywood, California.
是从加州北好莱坞的联合制冰公司运来的。

1075
00:47:23.660 --> 00:47:28.240
They put it through the industrial wood chipper device, and it sprayed out as snow.
他们把冰放进工业碎木机里，喷出来就成了雪。

1076
00:47:28.240 --> 00:47:30.360
So, I appreciate this.
所以我很欣赏这一点。

1077
00:47:30.460 --> 00:47:37.980
I mean, we filmed this in Southern California, but we knew that this would be airing in a Pennsylvania winter time frame.
我的意思是，我们是在南加州拍摄的，但我们知道这集会在宾夕法尼亚的冬天播出。

1078
00:47:37.980 --> 00:47:40.340
And so, we put these little details in.
所以，我们加入了这些小细节。

1079
00:47:40.440 --> 00:47:40.860
Well done.
干得漂亮。

1080
00:47:41.040 --> 00:47:41.980
I love it, too.
我也很喜欢。

1081
00:47:42.340 --> 00:47:43.600
Paints the picture, guys.
这画面感十足，伙计们。

1082
00:47:44.240 --> 00:47:50.600
Well, ultimately, Dwight and Ryan decide they're going to reach out to Nick, the IT guy.
总之，德怀特和瑞安决定去联系IT男尼克。

1083
00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:52.300
Make him their pawn.
把他当成棋子。

1084
00:47:52.780 --> 00:47:54.740
Help him bring down Jim.
帮他们搞垮吉姆。

1085
00:47:55.140 --> 00:47:55.460
Yeah.
没错。

1086
00:47:55.460 --> 00:48:04.140
Back in the office, Erin is helping Michael try and get all his toys onto the desk.
回到办公室，艾琳正在帮迈克尔把他的所有玩具摆到桌子上。

1087
00:48:04.680 --> 00:48:05.980
But she's having trouble.
但她遇到了点麻烦。

1088
00:48:06.140 --> 00:48:07.440
There's not as many surfaces.
桌面的空间不够多。

1089
00:48:07.920 --> 00:48:10.560
I want to point out two things in this scene.
我想指出这个场景里的两件事。

1090
00:48:10.760 --> 00:48:18.700
At 11 minutes, 57 seconds, there's a really good shot of the giraffe pen in my cup holder on my desk.
在11分57秒，能很清楚地看到我桌上笔筒里的长颈鹿圆珠笔。

1091
00:48:18.860 --> 00:48:19.700
The wonky one.
那个歪歪扭扭的。

1092
00:48:19.780 --> 00:48:20.540
The wonky giraffe.
那只歪脖子长颈鹿。

1093
00:48:20.560 --> 00:48:21.260
That never worked.
它从来就没好用过。

1094
00:48:21.440 --> 00:48:22.480
That never worked.
它从来就没好用过。

1095
00:48:22.480 --> 00:48:23.440
That you still have.
你现在还留着它。

1096
00:48:23.560 --> 00:48:24.560
That I still have.
我还留着它。

1097
00:48:24.700 --> 00:48:25.080
Aw.
噢。

1098
00:48:25.460 --> 00:48:31.420
So, if you want a good shot of it, it was a lot harder to see when it was at reception, but it's really good to see in this scene.
所以，如果你想看个特写，它在接待处时很难看清，但在这一幕里看得非常清楚。

1099
00:48:31.580 --> 00:48:32.500
Wonky giraffe.
歪脖子长颈鹿。

1100
00:48:32.980 --> 00:48:38.480
I also want to say how much I loved having Steve Carell at this desk clump.
我还想说，我有多喜欢史蒂夫·卡瑞尔坐在这一组办公桌旁。

1101
00:48:38.620 --> 00:48:43.660
It took us about a half a day to shoot all the scenes with Steve out in the bullpen.
我们花了大约半天时间，在办公区拍完了所有史蒂夫的戏份。

1102
00:48:43.660 --> 00:48:45.280
It was a delight.
那真是太棒了。

1103
00:48:45.620 --> 00:48:47.020
I absolutely loved it.
我非常喜欢。

1104
00:48:47.120 --> 00:48:47.980
He loved it.
他也乐在其中。

1105
00:48:47.980 --> 00:48:49.480
We got to be together.
我们能待在一起。

1106
00:48:49.920 --> 00:48:51.120
It was so fun.
真的太有趣了。

1107
00:48:51.540 --> 00:48:53.120
I would be so tickled.
我会感到非常高兴。

1108
00:48:53.260 --> 00:48:55.880
If he ever had to sit over in accounting, he'd be so tickled.
如果他哪天得坐在会计部，他一定会乐坏的。

1109
00:48:55.880 --> 00:48:56.380
Yes, right?
是啊，对吧？

1110
00:48:56.380 --> 00:48:56.860
He's so tickled.
他乐得不行。

1111
00:48:57.180 --> 00:48:57.660
Exactly.
没错。

1112
00:48:58.420 --> 00:49:01.320
Aaron's going to enter Jim's office with ants on a log.
亚伦要带着“蚂蚁上树”走进吉姆的办公室了。

1113
00:49:02.580 --> 00:49:09.200
You really get some insight into the things that Michael has convinced Aaron to do for him.
你真的能从中看出迈克尔说服亚伦为他做了些什么。

1114
00:49:09.440 --> 00:49:11.460
None of which Pam would have ever done.
这些事帕姆是绝对不会做的。

1115
00:49:11.580 --> 00:49:11.920
No.
没错。

1116
00:49:12.040 --> 00:49:13.560
They have a whole different relationship.
他们的关系完全不同。

1117
00:49:13.820 --> 00:49:22.160
And she so earnestly, like, believes in Michael's just, I don't know what, in his, she looks up to him.
她非常真诚地，怎么说呢，相信迈克尔的……我不知道该怎么形容，她很崇拜他。

1118
00:49:22.160 --> 00:49:22.600
Right.
确实。

1119
00:49:22.720 --> 00:49:26.580
I think she believes that he really does have this handbook on how to be a boss.
我想她真的相信迈克尔有一本关于如何当好老板的指南。

1120
00:49:26.600 --> 00:49:27.380
And this is what you do.
而这就是你该做的。

1121
00:49:27.480 --> 00:49:29.640
You bring ants on a log every day at 2 o'clock.
每天下午两点带一份“蚂蚁上树”。

1122
00:49:29.760 --> 00:49:31.800
You also have to get spun in your chair.
你还得坐在椅子上转圈。

1123
00:49:31.940 --> 00:49:32.360
Spun in a chair.
坐在椅子上转圈。

1124
00:49:32.360 --> 00:49:34.540
Because a spinning brain is a working brain.
因为转动的大脑才是工作的大脑。

1125
00:49:34.940 --> 00:49:35.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1126
00:49:35.980 --> 00:49:36.940
Ants on a log, guys.
伙计们，蚂蚁上树。

1127
00:49:37.160 --> 00:49:39.400
Celery stock, some peanut butter, and a few raisins.
芹菜杆，抹点花生酱，再放几颗葡萄干。

1128
00:49:39.540 --> 00:49:39.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1129
00:49:40.760 --> 00:49:41.300
That's it.
就是这样。

1130
00:49:41.360 --> 00:49:42.100
It's a great snack.
这可是很棒的零食。

1131
00:49:42.440 --> 00:49:43.280
It's a great snack.
这可是很棒的零食。

1132
00:49:43.660 --> 00:49:47.060
Have you ever done it where instead of raisins, you put chocolate chips?
你试过把葡萄干换成巧克力豆吗？

1133
00:49:47.680 --> 00:49:51.520
Oh, I'd probably like that better because I love chocolate with peanut butter.
噢，我可能会更喜欢那样，因为我超爱巧克力配花生酱。

1134
00:49:51.660 --> 00:49:51.880
Right?
对吧？

1135
00:49:52.160 --> 00:49:52.480
Oh.
噢。

1136
00:49:52.780 --> 00:49:53.380
It's real good.
真的很好吃。

1137
00:49:53.580 --> 00:49:55.180
Does the celery throw you off, though?
不过芹菜不会让你觉得奇怪吗？

1138
00:49:55.480 --> 00:49:56.000
No.
不会。

1139
00:49:56.260 --> 00:49:59.020
It still has that crisp, refreshing crunch.
它依然保持着那种清脆爽口的口感。

1140
00:49:59.400 --> 00:49:59.920
Okay.
好吧。

1141
00:50:00.540 --> 00:50:02.980
Well, Michael's going to blow his train horn.
迈克尔要吹他的火车汽笛了。

1142
00:50:03.320 --> 00:50:03.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1143
00:50:04.320 --> 00:50:06.180
And say that he got a new client.
还要宣布他签下了一个新客户。

1144
00:50:06.180 --> 00:50:08.220
And he instantly gets shade for this.
他立刻就遭到了大家的冷嘲热讽。

1145
00:50:08.320 --> 00:50:10.780
People are like, we don't really announce when we get sales anymore.
大家都在说，我们现在已经不搞这种签单宣告仪式了。

1146
00:50:10.780 --> 00:50:12.800
We haven't done that since 1992.
我们从1992年起就不这么干了。

1147
00:50:13.420 --> 00:50:14.300
I mean, come on.
我是说，拜托。

1148
00:50:14.800 --> 00:50:17.180
So this scene continued, Jenna.
所以这场戏还在继续，珍娜。

1149
00:50:17.380 --> 00:50:18.820
It's in the shooting draft.
它在拍摄剧本里。

1150
00:50:19.000 --> 00:50:21.180
It didn't make it in the final episode.
但最终没能剪进正片里。

1151
00:50:21.180 --> 00:50:22.740
But I thought it was really cute.
但我当时觉得那真的很可爱。

1152
00:50:23.200 --> 00:50:24.260
Michael is annoyed.
迈克尔很恼火。

1153
00:50:24.260 --> 00:50:27.180
So he goes, well, I guess I'll just celebrate with a snack then.
于是他说，好吧，那我想我还是吃点零食庆祝一下吧。

1154
00:50:27.640 --> 00:50:28.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1155
00:50:28.120 --> 00:50:29.260
And he walks into the kitchen.
然后他走进厨房。

1156
00:50:29.760 --> 00:50:35.980
And then you see sort of like this argument between Oscar and Michael, like, through the
接着你可以透过厨房门，看到奥斯卡和迈克尔之间发生了某种争执。

1157
00:50:35.980 --> 00:50:36.600
kitchen door.
厨房门。

1158
00:50:36.600 --> 00:50:38.960
And then Michael storms out.
然后迈克尔气冲冲地走了出来。

1159
00:50:39.000 --> 00:50:40.800
And they're having this heated conversation.
他们正在进行一场激烈的谈话。

1160
00:50:40.800 --> 00:50:43.780
And Michael's like, you know how long it took for those to freeze?
迈克尔说，你知道那些东西冻住要花多长时间吗？

1161
00:50:44.100 --> 00:50:50.700
And we see that Oscar has a little orange cube on, like, a toothpick, like a homemade
我们看到奥斯卡牙签上插着一个小橙色方块，就像自制的

1162
00:50:50.700 --> 00:50:51.340
popsicle.
冰棒一样。

1163
00:50:51.600 --> 00:50:55.380
Oh, like in the ice tray where you put orange juice in your ice tray?
哦，就像把橙汁倒进冰格里那样？

1164
00:50:55.560 --> 00:50:55.980
Yes.
没错。

1165
00:50:56.100 --> 00:50:56.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1166
00:50:56.660 --> 00:50:58.000
So Michael's furious.
所以迈克尔非常愤怒。

1167
00:50:58.000 --> 00:51:01.660
And Oscar's like, that's because you kept opening the freezer door to check on them.
奥斯卡说，那是因为你一直打开冰箱门去查看它们。

1168
00:51:01.660 --> 00:51:04.060
And Michael goes, yeah, but then I didn't check on them.
迈克尔说，是啊，但后来我没再查看了。

1169
00:51:04.140 --> 00:51:05.260
And now they're all gone.
结果现在全没了。

1170
00:51:05.260 --> 00:51:06.620
And the camera widens.
镜头拉开。

1171
00:51:06.700 --> 00:51:09.600
And we see Creed and Meredith each eating one.
我们看到克里德和梅雷迪思每人都在吃一个。

1172
00:51:09.840 --> 00:51:13.620
Everyone is eating Michael's homemade orange juice popsicles.
大家都在吃迈克尔自制的橙汁冰棒。

1173
00:51:13.820 --> 00:51:15.620
And he's furious about it.
他对此感到非常愤怒。

1174
00:51:15.880 --> 00:51:18.100
It was just this little runner that got cut.
这只是个被剪掉的小插曲。

1175
00:51:18.240 --> 00:51:19.720
And then he goes and sits down.
然后他走过去坐下。

1176
00:51:19.760 --> 00:51:21.120
And he smells the smell.
接着他闻到了那股味道。

1177
00:51:21.660 --> 00:51:23.160
Oh, the smell.
哦，那股味道。

1178
00:51:23.720 --> 00:51:24.200
Yes.
没错。

1179
00:51:24.200 --> 00:51:27.280
So he's not having a very good day in the bullpen.
所以他在办公区过得并不顺心。

1180
00:51:27.720 --> 00:51:28.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1181
00:51:28.540 --> 00:51:32.180
We find out that there is a kind of sulfur-like smell.
我们发现有一种类似硫磺的味道。

1182
00:51:32.400 --> 00:51:36.500
It is a side effect of Phyllis's new allergy medication.
这是菲利斯新吃的过敏药的副作用。

1183
00:51:36.760 --> 00:51:38.020
She sent an email about it.
她为此发过邮件。

1184
00:51:38.060 --> 00:51:38.420
She did.
确实发过。

1185
00:51:38.500 --> 00:51:39.980
And everyone seems fine with it.
而且大家似乎都对此没意见。

1186
00:51:40.320 --> 00:51:44.340
Even though Andy has tissues up his nose, he's just anticipating a nosebleed.
尽管安迪鼻子里塞着纸巾，他只是在预感会流鼻血。

1187
00:51:44.480 --> 00:51:45.680
This is it for Michael.
这对迈克尔来说是压死骆驼的最后一根稻草。

1188
00:51:45.940 --> 00:51:50.600
He cannot believe he's out in the bullpen where you don't celebrate a sale.
他无法相信自己待在这样一个办公区，没人庆祝销售业绩。

1189
00:51:50.600 --> 00:51:55.160
People are taking your homemade orange juice ice cube popsicles.
人们还拿走了他自制的橙汁冰块冰棒。

1190
00:51:55.520 --> 00:51:57.160
And there's a sulfur smell.
而且还有一股硫磺味。

1191
00:51:57.240 --> 00:51:57.920
And it's stinky.
臭烘烘的。

1192
00:51:58.180 --> 00:52:00.120
And he can't fit his things on his desk.
而且他的东西在桌子上都放不下了。

1193
00:52:00.540 --> 00:52:03.960
I also want to point out something else in this scene, actually.
其实我还想指出这一幕里的另一件事。

1194
00:52:04.180 --> 00:52:06.540
It's at 16 minutes and 7 seconds.
在16分07秒的时候。

1195
00:52:06.540 --> 00:52:12.320
There is a really good shot of the three hamster dolls on Michael's desk.
迈克尔桌上有三个仓鼠玩偶，那个镜头拍得非常好。

1196
00:52:12.740 --> 00:52:17.100
And the reason I point this out, I think we shared this a long time ago.
我之所以指出这一点，是因为我想我们很久以前就分享过。

1197
00:52:17.100 --> 00:52:22.660
But back when we shot the pilot, John Krasinski toured a paper company in Scranton.
但在拍摄试播集时，约翰·卡拉辛斯基去斯克兰顿的一家造纸公司参观过。

1198
00:52:22.800 --> 00:52:24.600
The manager there was a woman.
那里的经理是一位女士。

1199
00:52:24.740 --> 00:52:28.220
And she had a little stuffed hamster on her desk.
她的桌上有一个小仓鼠毛绒玩具。

1200
00:52:28.460 --> 00:52:35.900
And so Michael's little hamster toys are a nod to that little bit of research that John Krasinski did.
所以迈克尔桌上的小仓鼠玩具，是对约翰·卡拉辛斯基所做的那点调研的致敬。

1201
00:52:36.060 --> 00:52:39.220
And I just love that we have kept this detail going.
我特别喜欢我们一直保留着这个细节。

1202
00:52:39.540 --> 00:52:40.400
All these years.
这么多年了。

1203
00:52:40.480 --> 00:52:40.860
Yes.
没错。

1204
00:52:41.060 --> 00:52:42.540
I remember it was so important to Greg.
我记得这对格雷格来说非常重要。

1205
00:52:42.700 --> 00:52:44.880
He was like, no, we need the hamsters dressed up.
他当时说，不行，我们得给仓鼠穿上衣服。

1206
00:52:44.880 --> 00:52:46.580
Yeah, we need little dressed up ham.
对，我们需要穿上衣服的小仓鼠。

1207
00:52:46.640 --> 00:52:48.560
And everyone's like, what is this detail?
大家都问，这是什么细节啊？

1208
00:52:48.780 --> 00:52:49.760
He's like, I need it.
他说，我就是需要它。

1209
00:52:49.860 --> 00:52:51.440
It was like part of that authenticity.
这就像是真实感的一部分。

1210
00:52:51.440 --> 00:52:54.480
He loved spotting that in that video that John showed him.
他很喜欢在约翰给他看的那个视频里发现这一点。

1211
00:52:55.220 --> 00:52:56.260
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1212
00:52:56.420 --> 00:52:58.580
Angela, I just saw one more thing I didn't mention.
安吉拉，我刚才又发现了一件没提到的事。

1213
00:52:58.740 --> 00:53:02.560
There's a lot to unpack in these scenes where Michael is sitting out in the bullpen.
迈克尔坐在办公区外面的这些场景里，有很多值得深挖的地方。

1214
00:53:02.760 --> 00:53:05.700
There was a fan catch from Page M in Utica, New York.
有一位来自纽约尤蒂卡市的粉丝佩奇·M发现了这个。

1215
00:53:06.560 --> 00:53:10.920
When Michael announces his sale, Jim's door is closed in the background.
当迈克尔宣布他的销售业绩时，背景里吉姆的办公室门是关着的。

1216
00:53:10.960 --> 00:53:13.460
But then it's open at the end of the scene.
但场景结束时门又开了。

1217
00:53:13.460 --> 00:53:15.520
It's another thing like the hair mess up.
这就像头发弄乱了那个细节一样。

1218
00:53:16.560 --> 00:53:19.060
I love all the background catches, you guys.
伙计们，我喜欢所有这些背景细节。

1219
00:53:19.280 --> 00:53:20.080
Good catch, Paige.
发现得好，佩奇。

1220
00:53:20.860 --> 00:53:22.860
Kelly is now going to read Andy's card.
凯莉现在要读安迪的卡片了。

1221
00:53:23.000 --> 00:53:26.700
It's one of those cards, you guys, that you buy, and it has a whole message written in it.
伙计们，这就是那种你买的时候，里面已经写好了一整段话的卡片。

1222
00:53:26.820 --> 00:53:26.980
Yes.
是的。

1223
00:53:26.980 --> 00:53:27.100
You know?
你知道吧？

1224
00:53:27.860 --> 00:53:29.040
Here's what it says.
上面是这么写的。

1225
00:53:29.040 --> 00:53:32.200
You brighten my day with the sound of your voice.
你的声音照亮了我的每一天。

1226
00:53:32.400 --> 00:53:34.860
You bring so much laughter and love.
你带来了如此多的欢笑与爱。

1227
00:53:35.100 --> 00:53:36.660
You're everything to me.
你是我的一切。

1228
00:53:36.780 --> 00:53:40.820
And I was so blessed when God sent you here to me.
当上帝把你送到我身边时，我感到无比幸福。

1229
00:53:41.020 --> 00:53:43.920
To which Erin says, geez Louise.
对此艾琳说，天哪。

1230
00:53:44.600 --> 00:53:49.420
Yeah, then she has a talking head where she says she just can't compete with Kelly.
对，然后她有个采访镜头，说她根本没法和凯莉竞争。

1231
00:53:50.140 --> 00:53:51.400
Kelly can sing.
凯莉会唱歌。

1232
00:53:51.620 --> 00:53:52.260
She can dance.
她会跳舞。

1233
00:53:52.420 --> 00:53:54.280
She gets all of her clothes at the mall.
她的衣服都是在商场买的。

1234
00:53:54.800 --> 00:53:59.020
I mean, it makes total sense to her that Andy would pick Kelly.
我是说，在她看来，安迪会选凯莉完全说得通。

1235
00:53:59.700 --> 00:54:06.420
I mean, if you're looking at the two cards and you don't know anything about Snoopy or Woodstock, Kelly's card is beautiful.
我的意思是，如果你看着这两张卡片，又对史努比或伍德斯托克一无所知，凯莉的那张卡片确实很漂亮。

1236
00:54:06.800 --> 00:54:07.300
It is.
确实是。

1237
00:54:07.760 --> 00:54:09.640
Andy said he had no idea what was on the card.
安迪说他根本不知道卡片上写了什么。

1238
00:54:09.900 --> 00:54:16.880
No, he clearly picked out Erin's card and then just, like, quickly grabbed a bunch of others and handed them out randomly.
没错，他显然是挑了艾琳的那张，然后随手抓了一堆其他的，随机发了出去。

1239
00:54:16.880 --> 00:54:19.480
Yeah, for all we know, Kevin got a similar card.
是啊，说不定凯文也收到了类似的卡片呢。

1240
00:54:19.760 --> 00:54:20.000
True.
也是。

1241
00:54:20.480 --> 00:54:21.600
With no candy.
而且还没糖果。

1242
00:54:22.260 --> 00:54:25.320
I don't know if you noticed the location of Erin's talking head.
不知道你们有没有注意到艾琳采访镜头的位置。

1243
00:54:25.480 --> 00:54:29.420
She couldn't be in the conference room because that's where Jo and her Great Danes are.
她没法在会议室里，因为乔和她的丹麦大猎犬在那儿。

1244
00:54:29.680 --> 00:54:35.620
So we would set up an alternate talking head spot outside of the break room.
所以我们会在休息室外面设置一个临时的采访点。

1245
00:54:35.740 --> 00:54:36.140
Yes.
对。

1246
00:54:36.140 --> 00:54:40.920
There's a little hallway and many talking heads would happen there.
那儿有个小走廊，很多采访镜头都是在那儿拍的。

1247
00:54:40.980 --> 00:54:42.520
But that's why there's a plant.
所以那儿才会有盆栽。

1248
00:54:42.820 --> 00:54:43.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1249
00:54:43.220 --> 00:54:47.320
If you see a plant in a talking head, we're probably in that break room hallway.
如果你在采访镜头里看到盆栽，那我们大概就是在休息室走廊里。

1250
00:54:48.460 --> 00:54:57.540
Speaking of the break room, Dwight and Ryan are going to find Nick in there, Nick the IT guy, and they're kind of going to, like, do a shakedown.
说到休息室，德怀特和瑞安要在里面找尼克，就是那个IT男尼克，他们打算对他进行一番盘问。

1251
00:54:57.640 --> 00:54:58.240
Is that what it's called?
是叫这个名字吗？

1252
00:54:58.420 --> 00:55:00.040
Yeah, I think it is, a shakedown.
对，我想是，敲诈勒索。

1253
00:55:00.180 --> 00:55:02.300
I don't know if that's the right term, but basically they're, like—
我不知道这词用得对不对，但基本上他们就是……

1254
00:55:02.300 --> 00:55:07.100
It is the right term because I just watched an episode of Abbott Elementary, and they have a whole plot line about shakedowns.
这词用得对，因为我刚看了集《小学风云》，里面有一整条剧情线就是讲敲诈勒索的。

1255
00:55:07.140 --> 00:55:08.580
Okay, so there's a shakedown.
好吧，所以这就是敲诈勒索。

1256
00:55:08.700 --> 00:55:09.560
I learned something.
我学到了新东西。

1257
00:55:09.740 --> 00:55:10.460
There you have it.
就是这样。

1258
00:55:10.460 --> 00:55:17.560
But they're basically like, Nick, you're going to help us get Jim's password to his computer, and if you don't, we're going to do these kind of things.
但他们基本上就是说，尼克，你要帮我们拿到吉姆电脑的密码，如果你不帮，我们就会做这些事。

1259
00:55:17.700 --> 00:55:20.220
And then Ryan has to struggle to crush a can, yes?
然后瑞安得费劲去捏扁一个易拉罐，对吧？

1260
00:55:20.380 --> 00:55:22.900
But then Dwight completely crushes an apple.
但接着德怀特直接把一个苹果捏碎了。

1261
00:55:23.220 --> 00:55:23.500
Yeah.
没错。

1262
00:55:23.700 --> 00:55:25.820
We got a fan question from Laura S.
我们收到一个来自劳拉·S的粉丝提问。

1263
00:55:25.980 --> 00:55:26.560
in Australia.
她来自澳大利亚。

1264
00:55:26.940 --> 00:55:29.080
How did Rain crush the apple?
雷恩是怎么捏碎那个苹果的？

1265
00:55:29.400 --> 00:55:32.260
Was it a fakie apple, or is he just super strong?
那是假苹果，还是他力气真的那么大？

1266
00:55:33.040 --> 00:55:38.300
Her Randy Cordray, Dwight's crushing of the apple, was just real.
兰迪·科德雷说，德怀特捏碎苹果那段是真的。

1267
00:55:38.300 --> 00:55:40.280
They used a real apple.
他们用的是真苹果。

1268
00:55:40.700 --> 00:55:42.980
He said they did a bunch of practice runs.
他说他们排练了好多次。

1269
00:55:43.200 --> 00:55:46.640
They didn't drill any holes in it or, like, help him a little.
他们没在苹果上钻孔，也没给他提供什么帮助。

1270
00:55:46.820 --> 00:55:54.520
Okay, so they did kind of score the backside of the apple so that it could break away more easily, but they didn't do anything to the front.
好吧，他们确实在苹果背面划了几道，让它更容易裂开，但正面什么都没动。

1271
00:55:54.520 --> 00:55:55.440
It's a real apple.
那是真苹果。

1272
00:55:55.440 --> 00:56:06.160
He said Rain's fingertips were just strong enough to dig into the front of the apple, and then it broke away because of some of the scoring on the back.
他说雷恩的指尖力气足够大，能抠进苹果正面，然后因为背面的划痕，苹果就裂开了。

1273
00:56:06.320 --> 00:56:11.800
But, I mean, just that part, the part where they go into the front is really impressive.
但我是说，光是那一部分，也就是手指抠进苹果正面的那部分，真的让人印象深刻。

1274
00:56:11.800 --> 00:56:13.280
Good job, Rain.
干得好，雷恩。

1275
00:56:13.480 --> 00:56:13.920
Who knew?
谁能想到呢？

1276
00:56:15.160 --> 00:56:16.700
You know, that's the thing.
你知道，这就是问题所在。

1277
00:56:16.940 --> 00:56:27.740
Like, as an actor, especially being a television actor, because they generate scripts on an ongoing basis, and they'll just write something, and suddenly you're like,
作为一名演员，尤其是电视剧演员，因为剧本是持续创作的，他们会突然写出一些情节，然后你就会想，

1278
00:56:27.740 --> 00:56:31.780
Oh, I guess this week I'm skateboarding.
噢，看来这周我要玩滑板了。

1279
00:56:31.920 --> 00:56:33.680
I've never been on a skateboard before.
我以前从没玩过滑板。

1280
00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:39.020
And then you have, like, one week to figure out how to be a good enough skateboarder to pull off whatever they've written.
然后你只有一周的时间去琢磨怎么成为一个足够好的滑板手，来完成他们写出的戏份。

1281
00:56:39.400 --> 00:56:45.020
And in this case, like, how lucky are they that Rain could crush an apple with his fingertips?
在这种情况下，雷恩能用指尖捏碎苹果，他们得有多幸运啊？

1282
00:56:45.020 --> 00:56:45.980
No one asked.
没人要求他这么做。

1283
00:56:47.000 --> 00:56:50.200
And then if he couldn't have done it, what would they have done?
如果他做不到，他们会怎么办？

1284
00:56:50.340 --> 00:56:51.720
Would they have rewritten it?
他们会重写剧本吗？

1285
00:56:51.820 --> 00:56:53.320
Would they have found a fakie apple?
他们会找个假苹果吗？

1286
00:56:53.500 --> 00:56:54.200
I don't know.
我不知道。

1287
00:56:55.300 --> 00:56:58.740
So, our romantic comedy is about to begin.
好了，我们的浪漫喜剧要开始了。

1288
00:57:00.960 --> 00:57:02.140
Kelly's at the copier.
凯莉在复印机旁。

1289
00:57:02.380 --> 00:57:02.540
Yep.
没错。

1290
00:57:03.300 --> 00:57:07.100
Andy walks up behind her, and she turns around and goes, Oh, you scared me.
安迪走到她身后，她转过身说，噢，你吓到我了。

1291
00:57:07.680 --> 00:57:09.140
I didn't see you there.
我没看见你在这儿。

1292
00:57:09.360 --> 00:57:12.660
I mean, she is laying it on so thick.
我是说，她表现得太刻意了。

1293
00:57:12.660 --> 00:57:16.580
She touches his arm, gives him a kiss on the cheek.
她摸了摸他的手臂，还在他脸颊上亲了一下。

1294
00:57:16.740 --> 00:57:17.920
He's so confused.
他困惑极了。

1295
00:57:17.920 --> 00:57:19.240
He's so confused.
他困惑极了。

1296
00:57:19.240 --> 00:57:22.760
And that's when Meredith comes up and goes, We saw the card you gave her.
就在这时，梅雷迪思走过来，说，我们看到你给她的卡片了。

1297
00:57:22.760 --> 00:57:24.760
You gave that to me, we'd be doing it.
你要是把那个给我，我们早就上床了。

1298
00:57:25.040 --> 00:57:25.420
I know.
我知道。

1299
00:57:25.600 --> 00:57:26.340
She said something like that.
她大概就是这么说的。

1300
00:57:26.800 --> 00:57:27.700
And he's like, What?
然后他一脸茫然，说，什么？

1301
00:57:28.260 --> 00:57:29.800
Now Andy's freaked out.
现在安迪吓坏了。

1302
00:57:29.800 --> 00:57:34.020
He realizes what has happened, and Erin has seen the whole thing.
他意识到发生了什么，而艾琳目睹了全过程。

1303
00:57:34.420 --> 00:57:34.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1304
00:57:35.760 --> 00:57:45.000
Meanwhile, Michael is going to walk into what is now Jim's office and say he wants his old job back because he cannot handle the farty dirt patch that is the sales floor.
与此同时，迈克尔打算走进吉姆现在的办公室，说他想拿回原来的职位，因为他受不了销售部那块像屁一样的脏地盘。

1305
00:57:45.000 --> 00:57:48.960
Oh, well, Jim says the grass is always greener.
哦，好吧，吉姆说草总是那边更绿。

1306
00:57:48.960 --> 00:57:50.840
And he's like, There's no grass out there.
然后迈克尔说，外面根本没有草。

1307
00:57:51.100 --> 00:57:53.080
It's just a farty dirt patch.
那只是一块像屁一样的脏地盘。

1308
00:57:53.500 --> 00:57:54.480
It's amazing.
太搞笑了。

1309
00:57:55.200 --> 00:57:57.200
Jim says, What do you want to do?
吉姆问，你想怎么做？

1310
00:57:57.520 --> 00:57:59.660
They have a very funny exchange here.
他们在这里有一段非常有趣的对话。

1311
00:57:59.840 --> 00:58:03.960
The difference between Michael's plan and Jim's plan is pretty amazing.
迈克尔的计划和吉姆的计划之间的差异真是绝了。

1312
00:58:04.160 --> 00:58:08.040
Michael's number one idea is let's make a sign that says it's opposite day.
迈克尔的首选方案是做一个写着“今天是反话日”的牌子。

1313
00:58:08.360 --> 00:58:08.740
I know.
我知道。

1314
00:58:08.940 --> 00:58:09.220
Done.
搞定。

1315
00:58:09.220 --> 00:58:10.060
Solved.
解决了。

1316
00:58:10.560 --> 00:58:11.320
I know.
我知道。

1317
00:58:11.500 --> 00:58:17.460
And what I love is that Jim's idea is they just walk in and tell Joe that they want to switch jobs.
我喜欢的是，吉姆的想法是他们直接走进去告诉乔他们想换工作。

1318
00:58:17.700 --> 00:58:23.820
But he has to put it in language Michael will understand by saying, Why don't we do it the lethal weapon way?
但他必须用迈克尔能理解的语言来说，比如“我们为什么不按《致命武器》的方式来呢？”

1319
00:58:23.940 --> 00:58:25.120
What happens in lethal weapon?
《致命武器》里发生了什么？

1320
00:58:25.240 --> 00:58:27.740
They just walk in and tell their boss what they want, right?
他们直接走进去告诉老板他们想要什么，对吧？

1321
00:58:28.140 --> 00:58:28.580
Yes.
是的。

1322
00:58:28.780 --> 00:58:29.880
The lethal weapon way.
《致命武器》的方式。

1323
00:58:29.880 --> 00:58:30.700
Let's do that.
我们就这么干。

1324
00:58:31.000 --> 00:58:31.920
So they do.
于是他们照做了。

1325
00:58:32.360 --> 00:58:34.600
They find Joe walking her dogs outside.
他们发现乔正在外面遛狗。

1326
00:58:35.040 --> 00:58:38.600
She really can't believe that two grown men haven't been able to figure this out.
她简直不敢相信两个成年男人竟然连这点事都搞不定。

1327
00:58:38.600 --> 00:58:41.000
Two grown-ass men is what she says.
她原话是“两个大男人”。

1328
00:58:42.800 --> 00:58:45.980
She gets a phone call in the middle of this exchange.
在这次交谈中，她接到了一个电话。

1329
00:58:46.140 --> 00:58:46.900
She's like, Fine.
她说，行吧。

1330
00:58:47.000 --> 00:58:47.460
My God.
天哪。

1331
00:58:47.600 --> 00:58:48.540
I don't care.
我不在乎。

1332
00:58:48.700 --> 00:58:50.980
Just stop meeting with me to talk about it.
别再找我谈这件事了。

1333
00:58:51.100 --> 00:58:53.460
And here, walk my dogs and don't ride them.
还有，帮我遛狗，别骑它们。

1334
00:58:53.740 --> 00:58:53.980
Yeah.
是啊。

1335
00:58:54.060 --> 00:58:55.360
A lot of people try to ride them.
很多人都想骑它们。

1336
00:58:55.660 --> 00:58:56.640
I bet they do.
我敢打赌确实如此。

1337
00:58:57.040 --> 00:58:59.140
We had a fan question from Catherine H.
我们收到一个来自科罗拉多州丹佛市凯瑟琳·H的粉丝提问，

1338
00:58:59.240 --> 00:59:01.680
in Denver, Colorado, who wanted to know,
她想知道，

1339
00:59:01.880 --> 00:59:03.600
where are the lines and don't ride them?
“别骑它们”这句台词是哪来的？

1340
00:59:03.600 --> 00:59:06.540
A lot of people try to ride them scripted or improvised.
很多人都想问这句是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的。

1341
00:59:06.920 --> 00:59:08.340
Guys, that was scripted.
伙计们，那是剧本写的。

1342
00:59:08.460 --> 00:59:10.560
The way she delivered that was so amazing.
她那句台词的表达方式真是太棒了。

1343
00:59:10.840 --> 00:59:11.680
I agree.
我同意。

1344
00:59:12.380 --> 00:59:13.260
Just perfection.
简直完美。

1345
00:59:13.600 --> 00:59:16.920
When I reread this shooting draft, like, everything is scripted.
当我重读这份拍摄剧本时，发现所有内容都是写好的。

1346
00:59:17.300 --> 00:59:20.320
Like, there are moments where I was like, Oh, was that someone going off script?
有些时刻我还在想，哦，那是有人脱稿了吗？

1347
00:59:20.460 --> 00:59:20.640
No.
并没有。

1348
00:59:20.820 --> 00:59:22.480
This was like all scripted.
这全都是剧本写好的。

1349
00:59:22.660 --> 00:59:24.280
Every little moment you see.
你看到的每一个小细节。

1350
00:59:24.580 --> 00:59:28.100
When Michael messes up Jim's hair earlier, I went to the script.
当迈克尔早些时候弄乱吉姆的头发时，我查了剧本。

1351
00:59:28.240 --> 00:59:30.500
I was like, Maybe that was Steve just playing around.
我当时心想，也许那是史蒂夫在开玩笑。

1352
00:59:30.720 --> 00:59:31.020
Nope.
并没有。

1353
00:59:31.160 --> 00:59:31.940
In the script.
剧本里写的。

1354
00:59:31.940 --> 00:59:32.700
Really?
真的吗？

1355
00:59:32.980 --> 00:59:33.140
Yep.
没错。

1356
00:59:33.280 --> 00:59:35.340
It says, Michael messes up Jim's hair.
上面写着，迈克尔弄乱了吉姆的头发。

1357
00:59:36.140 --> 00:59:41.060
Well, Andy's going to quickly make an announcement to the bullpen that he has sent an email saying,
嗯，安迪很快会向办公区宣布，他发了一封邮件说，

1358
00:59:41.200 --> 00:59:44.920
Look, if you think I like you because of this Valentine's card, I'm paraphrasing,
听着，如果你以为我因为这张情人节贺卡而喜欢你——我这是意译——

1359
00:59:45.060 --> 00:59:46.740
but basically, I don't like you.
但基本上就是，我不喜欢你。

1360
00:59:46.840 --> 00:59:47.180
Okay?
好吗？

1361
00:59:47.720 --> 00:59:48.060
Yeah.
嗯。

1362
00:59:48.320 --> 00:59:49.520
It meant nothing to me.
它对我来说毫无意义。

1363
00:59:49.640 --> 00:59:50.100
It meant nothing.
毫无意义。

1364
00:59:50.460 --> 00:59:52.280
Well, Kelly comes in wide open.
然后凯莉直接冲了进来。

1365
00:59:52.440 --> 00:59:52.820
Hey!
嘿！

1366
00:59:53.100 --> 00:59:53.340
Hey!
嘿！

1367
00:59:53.780 --> 00:59:54.420
Very nice.
非常好。

1368
00:59:54.800 --> 00:59:57.140
Kelly's mad because she's like, Do you not like me?
凯莉很生气，她质问说，你是不喜欢我吗？

1369
00:59:57.140 --> 00:59:59.080
I would have liked you so hard.
我本来会非常用心地喜欢你的。

1370
00:59:59.080 --> 01:00:01.840
And Andy tells Kelly, There's someone else.
然后安迪告诉凯莉，我有别人了。

1371
01:00:01.940 --> 01:00:02.740
But he won't say who.
但他没说那是谁。

1372
01:00:03.320 --> 01:00:03.820
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1373
01:00:04.300 --> 01:00:06.840
There was a deleted Andy talking head.
有一段安迪的采访被删减了。

1374
01:00:07.060 --> 01:00:08.280
Ooh, what did it say?
噢，他说了什么？

1375
01:00:08.560 --> 01:00:13.260
He said, I gave Kelly $50 and she promised to stop loving me.
他说，我给了凯莉50美元，她答应不再爱我了。

1376
01:00:13.760 --> 01:00:14.340
Okay.
好吧。

1377
01:00:16.020 --> 01:00:17.160
That's pretty great.
那真是太棒了。

1378
01:00:17.340 --> 01:00:20.600
But Aaron's happy now because it turned out Andy didn't like Kelly.
但亚伦现在很高兴，因为结果证明安迪并不喜欢凯莉。

1379
01:00:20.980 --> 01:00:24.060
And Michael is happy as well because he's back in his office.
迈克尔也很高兴，因为他回到了自己的办公室。

1380
01:00:24.440 --> 01:00:28.220
And Aaron has set up all of his gadgets and they're going to have a little dance party.
亚伦架好了他所有的设备，他们要开个小型舞会。

1381
01:00:28.600 --> 01:00:36.140
At 20 minutes, one second, Aaron activates Michael's little Casio keyboard and we hear two pieces of music.
在20分01秒时，亚伦启动了迈克尔那个卡西欧小键盘，我们听到了两段音乐。

1382
01:00:36.140 --> 01:00:42.100
Randy Cordray said they were loop tracks that were found by our sound supervisor, Bobby Maxton.
兰迪·科德雷说那是我们的音效主管鲍比·麦克斯顿找到的循环音轨。

1383
01:00:42.540 --> 01:00:47.420
We licensed those song loops in perpetuity and it cost $3,000.
我们永久买下了这些歌曲循环的版权，花了3000美元。

1384
01:00:48.160 --> 01:00:51.240
Well, Dwight is just delighted that Jim is no longer manager.
嗯，德怀特对吉姆不再担任经理感到非常高兴。

1385
01:00:51.460 --> 01:00:55.400
He rubs it in that his time as manager lasted four hours.
他嘲讽吉姆的经理任期只持续了四个小时。

1386
01:00:55.620 --> 01:00:58.100
Yeah, it's the shortest of any manager.
没错，这是所有经理里最短的。

1387
01:00:58.780 --> 01:01:01.040
He's holding a Sheetz coffee mug, by the way.
顺便说一句，他手里拿着一个Sheetz的咖啡杯。

1388
01:01:01.440 --> 01:01:01.880
Nice!
不错！

1389
01:01:01.880 --> 01:01:06.340
Yeah, Jim is going to take Dwight's tie and dip it in his coffee.
是的，吉姆要把德怀特的领带浸到他的咖啡里。

1390
01:01:06.820 --> 01:01:07.920
Oh, Jim.
噢，吉姆。

1391
01:01:08.500 --> 01:01:15.320
In the shooting draft, this scene continued and you see Jim back in the annex and Toby is writing him up.
在拍摄剧本中，这一幕还在继续，你看到吉姆回到了附楼，托比正在写他的违规记录。

1392
01:01:15.540 --> 01:01:15.960
What?
什么？

1393
01:01:16.200 --> 01:01:16.700
Yes!
没错！

1394
01:01:17.140 --> 01:01:23.740
And there's this B-roll and Jim has taken Dwight's phone and has put it in Jell-O and put it in the fridge.
还有一段空镜，吉姆拿走了德怀特的手机，把它放进果冻里，然后塞进了冰箱。

1395
01:01:24.080 --> 01:01:27.240
And Toby says, please don't make this a habit.
托比说，请不要养成这种习惯。

1396
01:01:27.540 --> 01:01:28.900
And Jim is just smiling.
而吉姆只是在微笑。

1397
01:01:29.220 --> 01:01:31.180
The pranks are coming back, guys!
恶作剧回归了，伙计们！

1398
01:01:31.880 --> 01:01:35.320
Well, everybody was very excited for this storyline.
嗯，大家对这个剧情线都非常兴奋。

1399
01:01:35.660 --> 01:01:46.680
The writers spoke about how, for a while, they really liked this storyline where Jim was having to be more ambitious, he was having to be in charge, be a little serious.
编剧们谈到，有一段时间他们真的很喜欢吉姆不得不变得更有野心、不得不负责任、变得严肃一点的剧情线。

1400
01:01:46.880 --> 01:01:51.760
But they really missed the dynamic between Jim and Dwight.
但他们真的很怀念吉姆和德怀特之间的那种互动关系。

1401
01:01:51.860 --> 01:01:55.040
This was something that was sacrificed because of this storyline.
这是因为这个故事情节而不得不做出的牺牲。

1402
01:01:55.300 --> 01:01:57.080
Now they were going to get to have it back.
现在他们终于可以把它找回来了。

1403
01:01:57.460 --> 01:01:57.620
Yeah.
没错。

1404
01:01:59.040 --> 01:02:07.880
Well, Dwight and Ryan congratulate themselves for dethroning Jim, even though they're not quite sure what it was that they did that contributed to this.
嗯，德怀特和瑞安为自己把吉姆拉下马而沾沾自喜，尽管他们并不确定自己到底做了什么才导致了这一结果。

1405
01:02:08.160 --> 01:02:13.260
You know, you're going to see them get into the elevator and they're happy and then they get out of the elevator and they're arguing.
你知道，你会看到他们走进电梯时很高兴，然后电梯门一开，他们就在争吵。

1406
01:02:13.260 --> 01:02:18.540
You know, they had to film those on two different days because, you know, the elevator doesn't really go anywhere.
你知道，他们必须在两天内分别拍摄这些镜头，因为电梯其实根本不会动。

1407
01:02:18.760 --> 01:02:19.180
Right, right.
对，对。

1408
01:02:19.420 --> 01:02:24.320
So they got into an elevator and then it was like a total other day where they did the leaving of the elevator.
所以他们走进电梯，然后完全是另一天拍摄的走出电梯的戏份。

1409
01:02:25.060 --> 01:02:26.040
Well, I loved it.
嗯，我很喜欢这个设计。

1410
01:02:26.140 --> 01:02:27.940
I loved how it's the misdirect, right?
我喜欢这种误导，对吧？

1411
01:02:28.040 --> 01:02:31.380
That these two are going to go for a drink and then the doors open and they're arguing.
这两个人本来要去喝一杯，结果门一开他们就在吵架。

1412
01:02:31.600 --> 01:02:33.100
Just one elevator ride later.
仅仅过了一次电梯行程而已。

1413
01:02:33.320 --> 01:02:35.200
It's only like a two-story building.
这栋楼也就两层高。

1414
01:02:35.340 --> 01:02:37.460
This is a short ride to get in a fight.
这趟电梯坐得够短的，居然还能吵起来。

1415
01:02:37.460 --> 01:02:37.510
Right.
没错。

1416
01:02:37.680 --> 01:02:41.060
The thing they're arguing about is what drink they're going to get to celebrate.
他们争论的内容是去喝什么酒庆祝。

1417
01:02:41.600 --> 01:02:43.780
Dwight says martini bars are pretentious.
德怀特说马提尼酒吧太做作了。

1418
01:02:44.020 --> 01:02:47.500
And then Ryan says, I'm not interested in anything I have to make myself.
然后瑞安说，我可不想喝那种还得我自己调的酒。

1419
01:02:47.740 --> 01:02:50.820
And Dwight's like, it's beet vodka and it's delicious.
德怀特就说，那是甜菜伏特加，味道好极了。

1420
01:02:51.540 --> 01:02:53.020
I will show you.
我会让你见识一下的。

1421
01:02:54.040 --> 01:02:56.920
I got curious if beet vodka was a real thing.
我很好奇甜菜伏特加是不是真的存在。

1422
01:02:57.100 --> 01:02:57.620
Is it?
是真的吗？

1423
01:02:58.000 --> 01:02:58.400
Okay.
好吧。

1424
01:02:58.400 --> 01:02:59.500
I looked this up online.
我在网上查了一下。

1425
01:02:59.640 --> 01:03:00.280
This is what I found.
这是我找到的结果。

1426
01:03:00.280 --> 01:03:08.040
There might be others, but I did find a vodka from Minnesota called BET, and there's a line over the E.
可能还有其他的，但我确实找到了一种来自明尼苏达州的伏特加，名字叫BET，E上面还有一横。

1427
01:03:08.380 --> 01:03:09.960
BET, beet vodka.
BET，甜菜伏特加。

1428
01:03:10.520 --> 01:03:16.280
It's Minnesota's first vodka distilled from 100% sugar beets.
这是明尼苏达州第一款用100%糖甜菜蒸馏而成的伏特加。

1429
01:03:16.520 --> 01:03:17.660
Sugar beets?
糖甜菜？

1430
01:03:17.660 --> 01:03:18.340
Yes.
是的。

1431
01:03:18.600 --> 01:03:26.480
I was not able to get that vodka in time, but I also read that you can make your own beet-infused vodka.
我没能及时买到那种伏特加，但我还读到你可以自己制作甜菜浸泡伏特加。

1432
01:03:26.480 --> 01:03:31.200
And I looked up the recipe, and I made it.
我查了食谱，然后我就做了。

1433
01:03:31.320 --> 01:03:32.300
You did not.
你没做吧。

1434
01:03:32.480 --> 01:03:33.000
I did.
我做了。

1435
01:03:33.160 --> 01:03:37.020
You made beet-infused vodka?
你做了甜菜浸泡伏特加？

1436
01:03:37.380 --> 01:03:37.980
Explain.
解释一下。

1437
01:03:38.360 --> 01:03:38.640
Okay.
好的。

1438
01:03:38.700 --> 01:03:41.900
I found a recipe on allrecipes.com.
我在allrecipes.com上找到了一个食谱。

1439
01:03:41.920 --> 01:03:44.580
This one is by Jonah Luck.
这是乔纳·勒克写的。

1440
01:03:44.740 --> 01:03:45.960
Giving you a shout-out, Jonah.
向你致敬，乔纳。

1441
01:03:46.260 --> 01:03:48.520
Here's the quote about this recipe.
这是关于这个食谱的评价。

1442
01:03:48.680 --> 01:03:53.120
This is a full-flavored and earthy vodka that will keep you coming back.
这是一款风味浓郁、带有泥土气息的伏特加，会让你回味无穷。

1443
01:03:53.120 --> 01:03:53.640
Hmm.
嗯。

1444
01:03:53.880 --> 01:03:57.540
The ingredients were two pounds of beets, peeled and cubed.
配料是两磅甜菜，去皮切块。

1445
01:03:57.720 --> 01:03:58.760
I went to the store.
我去了商店。

1446
01:03:58.960 --> 01:04:00.180
I bought a lot of beets.
我买了很多甜菜。

1447
01:04:00.360 --> 01:04:01.220
I peeled them.
我把它们削了皮。

1448
01:04:01.300 --> 01:04:02.120
My hands were red.
我的手都红了。

1449
01:04:02.220 --> 01:04:08.400
I was trying to hide them from you the other day on our edit because my hands were so stained from peeling these beets,
前几天剪辑的时候我一直试图向你隐瞒，因为我的手被削甜菜染得太红了，

1450
01:04:08.460 --> 01:04:11.200
and I cubed them and cut them in little squares on Monday.
周一的时候我把它们切成了小方块。

1451
01:04:11.460 --> 01:04:12.760
I have to stop you.
我得打断你一下。

1452
01:04:12.980 --> 01:04:13.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1453
01:04:13.620 --> 01:04:21.460
What was the reaction to the people in the store when Angela came in and bought two pounds of beets?
安吉拉去店里买了整整两磅甜菜时，店里的人是什么反应？

1454
01:04:21.460 --> 01:04:26.280
At the checkout line, the guy checking me out, you could see everything in him.
在结账排队时，那个给我结账的伙计，你能看穿他的一切心思。

1455
01:04:26.460 --> 01:04:28.940
It was like you could see the vein in his forehead.
就好像能看到他额头上的青筋一样。

1456
01:04:29.300 --> 01:04:32.320
He had to weigh the beets, and he was like, you're buying beets?
他得给甜菜称重，他那表情就像在说，你居然买甜菜？

1457
01:04:32.400 --> 01:04:32.980
And I was like, uh-huh.
我就回了句，嗯哼。

1458
01:04:33.040 --> 01:04:34.240
And he goes, uh-huh, uh-huh.
然后他回我，嗯哼，嗯哼。

1459
01:04:34.400 --> 01:04:36.840
Like, he so wanted to say something.
就好像他特别想说点什么。

1460
01:04:37.460 --> 01:04:41.000
Okay, so on Monday, I had to peel and cube the beets.
好了，周一的时候，我得把甜菜削皮切块。

1461
01:04:41.380 --> 01:04:42.940
It took an actual long time.
真的花了好长时间。

1462
01:04:42.940 --> 01:04:53.780
And then I had to get one liter of vodka, and I had to put the beets in a sealable container and pour vodka over the beets and shake it vigorously.
然后我得买一升伏特加，把甜菜放进密封容器里，倒入伏特加，然后用力摇晃。

1463
01:04:54.060 --> 01:04:58.320
Then I had to place the container in a cool, dark place and store it for three days.
接着我得把容器放在阴凉避光的地方，存放三天。

1464
01:04:58.480 --> 01:05:00.360
But twice a day, I had to go and shake it.
但每天还得去摇晃两次。

1465
01:05:01.220 --> 01:05:02.120
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1466
01:05:02.120 --> 01:05:05.320
This is what I've been doing all week, and I wanted to tell you.
我这一周都在忙这个，我一直想告诉你。

1467
01:05:05.560 --> 01:05:06.640
I brought them.
我把它们带来了。

1468
01:05:06.820 --> 01:05:11.960
I got individual little containers so we can all try my beet-infused vodka.
我准备了独立的小容器，这样我们大家都能尝尝我泡的甜菜伏特加。

1469
01:05:11.980 --> 01:05:14.060
I'm going to tell you, I tried it this morning.
我得先告诉你，我今天早上尝过了。

1470
01:05:14.060 --> 01:05:15.020
It is earthy.
味道很土。

1471
01:05:15.460 --> 01:05:15.880
Okay.
好吧。

1472
01:05:16.100 --> 01:05:16.460
It's earthy.
确实很土。

1473
01:05:16.700 --> 01:05:18.660
I documented making it all.
我把制作过程全记录下来了。

1474
01:05:18.800 --> 01:05:19.840
I'll put it in stories.
我会发到动态里。

1475
01:05:20.300 --> 01:05:24.320
Now, this is just, you don't do anything to the beets except cube them.
这个嘛，除了切块，你什么都不用对甜菜做。

1476
01:05:24.460 --> 01:05:27.520
Like, you didn't have to boil them or make them soft.
就是说，你不用煮熟或者弄软它们。

1477
01:05:27.600 --> 01:05:28.220
It's raw beet.
是生甜菜。

1478
01:05:28.220 --> 01:05:29.400
Yes, it's raw beets.
对，是生甜菜。

1479
01:05:29.460 --> 01:05:29.680
Okay.
好吧。

1480
01:05:29.740 --> 01:05:35.460
That's why I couldn't cheat and buy already, you know, because they had packages of steamed cubed beets.
所以我不能偷懒去买现成的，你知道吧，因为店里有那种包装好的蒸熟甜菜块。

1481
01:05:35.580 --> 01:05:36.820
But it's raw beets.
但必须是生甜菜。

1482
01:05:36.900 --> 01:05:37.440
Let's try it.
我们来尝尝吧。

1483
01:05:37.620 --> 01:05:42.460
This is also another nice way to say happy birthday.
这也是祝你生日快乐的另一种不错的方式。

1484
01:05:43.280 --> 01:05:46.780
Oh, guys, I have individual containers for you to take home.
哦，伙计们，我给你们每人准备了独立容器带回家。

1485
01:05:47.000 --> 01:05:48.600
So you're taking this home.
所以你们得把这个带回家。

1486
01:05:48.920 --> 01:05:50.600
Let's try some beet-infused vodka.
来尝尝甜菜伏特加吧。

1487
01:05:51.760 --> 01:05:52.700
All right, guys.
好了，伙计们。

1488
01:05:53.500 --> 01:05:56.100
It looks like a container of blood.
看起来像一罐血。

1489
01:05:56.360 --> 01:05:58.000
Things I never thought I would do.
我从没想过我会做这种事。

1490
01:05:58.460 --> 01:05:59.040
All right.
好了。

1491
01:05:59.300 --> 01:06:00.020
Wait, here we go.
等等，开始了。

1492
01:06:00.340 --> 01:06:01.480
The beet really comes through.
甜菜的味道真的很浓。

1493
01:06:01.960 --> 01:06:02.120
Okay.
好吧。

1494
01:06:02.120 --> 01:06:03.340
Okay, do you smell the beet?
好了，你们闻到甜菜味了吗？

1495
01:06:03.580 --> 01:06:04.360
I smell the beet.
我闻到了甜菜味。

1496
01:06:04.520 --> 01:06:05.700
It's as earthy as promised.
正如预期的那样，土味十足。

1497
01:06:05.900 --> 01:06:06.440
Okay, ready?
好了，准备好了吗？

1498
01:06:06.600 --> 01:06:07.000
Here we go.
开始了。

1499
01:06:07.040 --> 01:06:07.880
We're going to sip it.
我们要小酌一口。

1500
01:06:14.980 --> 01:06:16.880
It's exactly how I pictured it.
这和我预想的一模一样。

1501
01:06:17.040 --> 01:06:17.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1502
01:06:18.220 --> 01:06:20.360
That's a tub of beets that's soaking.
那是一桶正在浸泡的甜菜。

1503
01:06:20.440 --> 01:06:20.980
Now I'm getting the vodka aftertaste.
现在我尝到了伏特加的余味。

1504
01:06:22.520 --> 01:06:23.620
It's medicine-y.
有股药味。

1505
01:06:23.940 --> 01:06:25.600
It reminds me of a medicine.
让我想起了一种药。

1506
01:06:25.840 --> 01:06:26.700
Here is the thing.
重点是这个。

1507
01:06:26.920 --> 01:06:28.300
All you taste are beets.
你尝到的全是甜菜味。

1508
01:06:28.600 --> 01:06:30.120
So the vodka could sneak up on you.
所以伏特加可能会让你不知不觉就醉了。

1509
01:06:30.280 --> 01:06:31.160
But it's there.
但它确实在里面。

1510
01:06:31.740 --> 01:06:32.840
There you go, guys.
给你们，伙计们。

1511
01:06:32.840 --> 01:06:36.020
Dwight, this is like us having to drink at Shroop FarMs.
德怀特，这就像我们必须在施鲁特农场喝酒一样。

1512
01:06:36.480 --> 01:06:36.760
Yay.
耶。

1513
01:06:38.500 --> 01:06:40.620
What if we threw a Splenda in here?
如果我们往里面加点代糖会怎么样？

1514
01:06:40.960 --> 01:06:43.140
I feel like that's what it needs.
我觉得这正是它所需要的。

1515
01:06:43.140 --> 01:06:45.420
I'm going to make a Bloody Mary with this and report back.
我要用这个做一杯血腥玛丽，然后再向大家汇报。

1516
01:06:45.640 --> 01:06:47.780
Oh, there was a recipe for that.
哦，确实有个那样的食谱。

1517
01:06:47.780 --> 01:06:50.260
To make Bloody Marys with beet-infused vodka.
用甜菜浸泡的伏特加做血腥玛丽。

1518
01:06:50.640 --> 01:06:52.360
Oh, Sam, I have a much bigger container.
哦，萨姆，我有一个大得多的容器。

1519
01:06:52.600 --> 01:06:53.260
You can take it home.
你可以带回家。

1520
01:06:54.300 --> 01:06:54.620
Great.
太棒了。

1521
01:06:54.900 --> 01:06:55.380
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1522
01:06:55.960 --> 01:06:56.440
Yay.
耶。

1523
01:06:56.920 --> 01:06:57.940
Angela, this was delightful.
安吉拉，这太令人愉快了。

1524
01:06:57.940 --> 01:06:58.820
This is really was.
真的非常棒。

1525
01:06:58.880 --> 01:07:00.040
Thank you for making this.
谢谢你做这个。

1526
01:07:01.520 --> 01:07:03.240
You guys drink responsibly.
你们要负责任地喝酒。

1527
01:07:03.460 --> 01:07:05.560
This was a really fun thing to do, actually.
说实话，这真的很有趣。

1528
01:07:05.560 --> 01:07:06.540
I enjoyed it.
我很享受。

1529
01:07:06.660 --> 01:07:09.220
And I feel like Dwight would be proud, guys.
而且我觉得德怀特会为我们感到骄傲的，伙计们。

1530
01:07:09.680 --> 01:07:14.220
This is like, what's the name of those people who, like, mixologist level.
这就像，那些人叫什么来着，就是调酒师级别的。

1531
01:07:14.400 --> 01:07:14.880
Yes.
没错。

1532
01:07:14.880 --> 01:07:16.940
Kind of business here, and.
这种生意，而且。

1533
01:07:17.220 --> 01:07:21.260
I'm excited for on the way home when I get on the train beet drunk holding a plant that
我很期待在回家的路上，我能喝着甜菜伏特加，抱着一盆植物坐火车，

1534
01:07:21.260 --> 01:07:21.740
I can air to be us.
我可以假装是我们。

1535
01:07:21.840 --> 01:07:24.620
You're drinking your beet vodka with your succulent.
你正抱着你的多肉植物喝着甜菜伏特加。

1536
01:07:24.740 --> 01:07:24.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1537
01:07:24.900 --> 01:07:27.360
Well, you guys, that was manager and salesman.
好了，伙计们，以上就是经理和销售员的内容。

1538
01:07:27.560 --> 01:07:34.260
If you were keeping track of how many times the dogs went to Andy's crotch, he had those
如果你一直在记录那些狗靠近安迪胯部的次数，他那些狗，我是说，在整整五场戏里都待在那儿。

1539
01:07:34.260 --> 01:07:36.920
dogs, I mean, up in there for five full scenes.
那些狗，我是说，在整整五场戏里都待在那儿。

1540
01:07:37.220 --> 01:07:37.480
Wow.
哇。

1541
01:07:37.780 --> 01:07:40.180
That's quite a bit of time if you look at the whole episode.
如果你看看整集节目，那可是相当长的时间了。

1542
01:07:40.820 --> 01:07:47.360
Well, on that note, I guess we want to say thank you to Rainn Wilson, who I reached out
好了，说到这里，我想我们要感谢雷恩·威尔森，我为了这一集联系了他，还有兰迪·科德雷，以及为我们制作新鲜甜菜伏特加的安吉拉·金赛。

1543
01:07:47.360 --> 01:07:54.240
to for this episode, and Randy Cordray, and Angela Kinsey for making us fresh beet vodka.
感谢你，安吉拉。

1544
01:07:54.240 --> 01:07:55.320
Thank you, Angela.
不客气。

1545
01:07:55.640 --> 01:07:56.240
